<title>THAILAND: Thailand set to allow 150,000T corn imports.</title>
<headline>Thailand set to allow 150,000T corn imports.</headline>
<dateline>BANGKOK 1997-07-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Thailand is set to allow the feed industry to import an additional 150,000 tonnes of tariff-free corn for the rest of the year, a commerce ministry official said on Tuesday.  </p>
<p>The move was prompted by near-term shortages of corn supplies caused by an unseasonably late rainy season.</p>
<p>&quot;The ministry is expected to approve the plan very soon. What is being discussed now is the period that the corn would be imported,&quot; said an official who asked not to be named.</p>
<p>The government had earlier allowed 200,000 tonnes of corn imports under the same scheme.</p>
<p>    -- Bangkok newsroom (662) 652-0642   REUTER</p>
